{"retractions" [[17592186339811 :question/problem "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$"] [17592186339811 :question/worked-solution "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =\\frac{1}{y}\\,i-\\frac{1}{x}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\,j)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t\\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-2(2\\pi )-0 \\\\  & =-4\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186339813 17592186339814 17592186339815 17592186339816 17592186339817] "immutable_fields" [[17592186339812 :answer-field/id] [17592186339812 :answer-field/key] [17592186339812 :answer-field/type] [17592186339812 :answer-field/correct] [17592186339812 :answer-field/choices]]}
